thread_text:
maria_cs: quick heads-up — onboarding call w/ NorthLane. after hooking our web SDK they can auth, but as soon as they ramp traffic (approx 50–70 concurrent sessions) they see intermittent 403s then a bunch of 429s. they’re worried about hitting SLA for their renewal.

sam_engineer: can you paste the error payload and sdk version?

maria_cs: paste below (redacted):
```
{
  error: { code: 403, message: \"Invalid token: scope missing\" }
}
// then later
{
  error: { code: 429, message: \"rate_limit_exceeded\" }
}
```
using web-sdk v1.3.2 and ephemeral tokens via our popup flow.

alex_devops: two quick suspects: (1) token refresh window too short -> clients re-request a new token at same time causing fanout; (2) preflight/concurrent preflight on their CI/edge causing many parallel auth checks.

sam_engineer: agree. common pattern: client tries to refresh simultaneously -> thundering herd -> auth proxy returns 429 and then SDK surfaces 403 when token exchange fails. do they use short-lived ephemeral (<=60s)?

maria_cs: yes they set expiry 45s to be conservative.

sam_engineer: ok. immediate mitigation: bump ephemeral TTL to 5m for the ramp test, add jitter+linear backoff on refresh, and set client-side concurrency limit to 10 while we debug. here's a minimal js snippet to limit refreshes: 
```js
const sdk = new RedwoodSDK({ token: ephemeralToken, refreshOptions: { ttlBuffer: 30, jitter: true, maxConcurrency: 10 } });
// client-side: gate refresh with a single-flight mutex + randomized retry windows
```

alex_devops: also capture auth logs from their edge proxy for 280501*/requests. i can add a scatter plot for request timestamps to confirm simultaneous refresh spikes.

maria_cs: i'll ask NorthLane to run the small change and share logs. can we also do a temporary quota bump on their org to avoid spike-related 429s? they’re in the free trial/early onboarding bracket and want to prove sustained traffic for renewal.

lee_sales: customer mentioned renewal is contingent on hitting latency + uptime targets by EOM. if this drags, risk increases. recommend a short-term uplift (weekly) while we stabilize.

sam_engineer: i’ll do two things: (A) audit backend auth exchange for 5m window + search for concurrent token issuances; (B) add a transient rule to relax rate checks for this org for the next 72h (must be by ops approval). tagging prod-bot to record the change.

prod-bot: @sam_engineer — ops change request created: #CHG-2805-11. Approver needed: alex_devops.

alex_devops: approved. i'll open a 72h allowance and enable detailed tracing. sam, please share the exact org-id.

maria_cs: org-id: org_northlane_74. i’ll message them the client update + ask them to run a 10-min ramp with TTL=300s. will post logs here once done.

sam_engineer: action items: 1) maria -> coordinate customer test (today) 2) alex -> enable 72h relaxed rate window + tracing 3) sam -> audit token exchange and propose SDK patch for single-flight refresh (PR if needed) 4) lee -> note renewal risk and escalate to CSM weekly sync.

maria_cs: thanks all. i'll update thread after the run. :thumbsup:
